`offence under s 406` with `the Penang agent, not in the way of any trade, profession or business` 's `breach of trust`
not `offence under s 407` with `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`
not `offence under s 408` with `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`
not `offence under s 409` with `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`
`charge under s 409` with `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity` 's `refusal` is equal to A charge under section 409 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of criminal breach of trust by a public servant, or by a banker, merchant, agent, director, officer, partner, key executive or fiduciary (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: being entrusted with the property, or with dominion over it, in one of the capacities section 409(1) names — (a) as a public servant; (b) in the way of a trade, profession or business as a banker, merchant, factor, broker, attorney or agent; (c) in a professional capacity OTHER than one of those; (d) as a director of a corporation; (e) as an officer of an unincorporated association; (f) as a partner in a partnership; (g) as a key executive of a corporation, an unincorporated association or a partnership; or (h) as a fiduciary; committing criminal breach of trust in respect of that property (section 405) — run the section 406 charge on the same entrustment to see which of its elements failed.
